# Docs stay current

When you change code in this repo, update every doc that describes that code in the **same pass**. Do not leave a follow-up.

## What to touch

- `README.md` — user-facing behavior, build/run, install/`xattr`, settings, constraints
- `docs/architecture.md` — scheduling, calendar filtering, banner window, marquee, wake handling, launch-at-login

If a new user-facing behavior or architectural mechanism appears, add it to the matching doc. If a behavior is removed or renamed, delete or rewrite the stale claim.

## Consistency

- README and `docs/architecture.md` must not contradict each other.
- Docs must match the current codebase (types, timers, window flags, settings keys/labels, deployment target, arch).
- Do not invent features in docs that the code does not implement.
- Do not leave comments or docs that describe a previous design.

## Example

Code changes `Design.animationDuration` from 4.5s to 6s → update the duration stated in `docs/architecture.md` (and README if it mentions the number) in the same edit set.
